  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "In a Legends of Ren Zu stretch, Ren Zu sees a tiny white Gu fleeing a larger armored Gu. The white Gu hides behind him and begs to be saved, and that plea grows a new heart of sympathy in his chest. The armored Gu names itself strong Gu and the tiny Gu weak Gu, and states that the strong must eat the weak. Ren Zu refuses to hand Weak Gu over, and Strong Gu flies away after saying it will return.",
        "chapters": [
          2036
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu",
          "char_ren_zu",
          "gu_strong_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Cited chapters call it tiny and white while it flees and hides behind Ren Zu. They do not assign a cultivation rank or a living owner outside the legend telling.",
        "chapters": [
          2036
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-in-the-legend",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "When Strong Gu returns inside a huge Predicament, Weak Gu thanks Ren Zu for protection and proposes scaring the Predicament away by pretending to be strong. It tells him to use fear Gu and Attitude Gu, then to put Attitude Gu on self Gu so the disguise fools even himself. The Predicament does not flee, and Ren Zu concludes that a facade cannot solve a huge predicament. Through that contest Ren Zu still treats protecting Weak Gu as part of what he cannot afford to lose.",
        "chapters": [
          2041
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "disguise-advice",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_attitude_gu",
          "gu_self_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When Tribulations pour from the Predicament, Weak Gu flies with betrayal Gu and fear Gu and urges Ren Zu to run, then flees after Self Gu bites the three. Rules and Regulation Gu tell Self Gu not to chase them, and say Weak Gu and betrayal Gu cannot help in that moment.",
        "chapters": [
          2052
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "flight-under-tribulations",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_betrayal_gu",
          "gu_rules_and_regulation_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A later telling recalls that Ren Zu protected Weak Gu, and that Weak Gu urged him to put Attitude Gu on self Gu so the deception could fool even himself and the Predicament.",
        "chapters": [
          2184
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "flight-under-tribulations",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
